"type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row per verb — is claiming all ~47 of them, and the claim is easy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to half-keep: one line left unassigned means a plain modern narrator takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over on the turn after a re-voiced one, which is exactly the defect the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dungeon and Zork 1 floors were written to close. Naming each verb in a test","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"catches that; it does not catch a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"forty-eighth","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" stub arriving in the engine","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tomorrow, which would slip past every named assertion at once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So this reads the properties off ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameText.StubReplies","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than listing them: every line the engine actually ships is compared,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one added tomorrow is compared the day it lands. A property whose type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this cannot render is reported as its own issue rather than skipped, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what keeps “reflected” from quietly meaning “unchecked”.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That last sentence has no exception to it as of #246. ","type":"text"},{"code":"give","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" used to be one:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the one line about two objects, so not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameText.Line","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so unreachable by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection and compared by hand below the loop — the single line in here that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"could change shape without the sweep noticing. It takes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameText.Gift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"now, and goes through the same door as the other forty-eight.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Which sentences each line prints is the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"subject’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" business as of #255:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LineSubject.samples(one:many:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" supplies them, so a subject arriving","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tomorrow is swept the day it lands rather than after somebody teaches a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"switch here about it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is split out from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the sweep can be tested for being ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"alive","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": a reflection loop that matches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing passes silently, where one asserted to see all forty-nine lines","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"engineVoicedStubLines(in:)","symbolKind":"func","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"engineVoicedStubLines"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":":